-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat rep from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-seat-rep: the seat questions of Articles 1 to 4, 111 and 113 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744), asked by an authorised representative of a provider: a party located or established in the Union that has accepted a written mandate from a provider to carry out the Regulation's obligations and procedures on its behalf (Article 3(5)).
--
-- LAYER 2 (the seat layer). Every question below calls a function of the keel (aia-scope, aia-definitions, aia-literacy, aia-timeline, aia-annex-x) and restates no rule.
-- The keel decides what the text means, the date it applies from and which text is in force; this file asks, in the words and with the facts of this seat, what a person in the seat can state.
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it. The role facts are asked once, in the question under Article 3 (or Article 2 for a product manufacturer and a person affected),
-- and no other question asks them again; where a keel function needs the role as a fact, this file passes TRUE.
--
-- THE DATE ASKED. Every question whose answer depends on a date asks `the date asked`. It selects the text in force (the Regulation as enacted until 26 July 2026, as amended from 27 July 2026,
-- the day the Omnibus enters into force) and whether the provision applies yet (Chapter I from 2 February 2025; the group General from 2 August 2026).
-- The other shared inputs (the placement date, the significant-change flag, the route by which the AI system is high-risk) carry the same name and @desc in every question that needs them.
--
-- RESULTS. A MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE DATE answer of NOTHING means "not covered": the provision does not speak to these facts, or has not begun to apply, or is not in the text in force on the date asked.
-- JUST FALSE is the text's own "no" (a flat negative such as "does not apply", or a condition it states). The answer of a keel function is passed through unchanged; nothing here turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- An exported obligation (a DEONTIC answer) is shown by a form as the placeholder "<obligation>"; its content is read with #TRACE in the case file.
--
-- STATUS. Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect (it says so itself, line 2 of the file).
-- The readings are the keel's (NOTES.md, fork register) and this layer's (NOTES.md, fork register P0): assumed, not ruled by a lawyer.
-- The Interact form and jl4-service were not run; l4 check, l4 run and l4 batch were.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`
-- Chapter I (Articles 1 to 4a) applies from 2 February 2025 (Art 113 third paragraph, point (a)).
-- Article 1 itself creates no rule (a purpose clause and a statement of contents): the one question a seat asks of it is whether the Chapter it opens applies.

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1660 | (a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025, with the exception of Article 5(1), first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb), and Article 5(1a) and (1b) which shall apply from 2 December 2026;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202 | Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025;
@ref Art 113 first paragraph and third paragraph point (a): Chapter I (src:1656) (src:1660) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202)
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).
@export Under Article 1, as an authorised representative, does Chapter I apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 1, as an authorised representative, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Article 2(1): does the Regulation apply to me?`
-- Article 2(1) lists whom the Regulation applies to; a seat asks the limb that names its role.
-- A party outside every limb is "not covered" (NOTHING): the list does not close.

-- src:38 | (f) authorised representatives of providers, which are not established in the Union;
@ref Art 2(1)(f) (src:38)
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it, so the keel's role fact is passed as TRUE. Whether the definition of the role fits is asked once, in the question under Article 3.
@export Under Article 2(1)(f), as an authorised representative, does the Regulation apply to me as an authorised representative of a provider not established in the Union?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the provider I represent is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provider you represent established in the Union?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(1)(f), as an authorised representative, does the Regulation apply to me as an authorised representative of a provider not established in the Union` IS
    `Art 2(1)(f) the Regulation applies to the authorised representative of a provider not established in the Union` `the date asked` TRUE `the provider I represent is established in the Union`


§ `Article 2(2): my high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (replaced by the Omnibus)`
-- Only if the AI system is high-risk under Article 6(1) and related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I.
-- The answer names, for one Article at a time, whether it applies to such a system.

-- src:41 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply. Articles 57, 58 and 59 shall apply only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply. Article 57 applies only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
@ref Art 2(2) (src:41) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420)
-- The date asked selects the text: the list of Articles that apply is shorter as enacted (Articles 102 to 109) than as amended (Articles 102 to 112, and Article 60a).
-- The Article is asked as its number, the letter that may follow it (a for Article 60a) and a paragraph number (0 for the whole Article).
@export Under Article 2(2), as an authorised representative, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the AI system is related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I?
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation?
      `the number of the Article I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which Article of the Regulation do you ask about? Give its number, for example 9 for Article 9.
      `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any` IS A STRING @desc If the Article has a letter after its number, give it, for example a for Article 60a. Otherwise leave this empty.
      `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article` IS A NUMBER @desc Which paragraph of that Article do you ask about? Give its number, or 0 if you mean the whole Article.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(2), as an authorised representative, does the provision I name apply to my high-risk AI system with Section B products` IS
    `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the AI system is related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the provision I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the provision I ask about` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
            number IS `the number of the Article I ask about`
            letter IS `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any`
            paragraph IS `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article`


§ `Article 2(3): areas outside Union law, and military, defence and national security`
-- Only if the matter, the AI system or its output is in one of these areas.

-- src:44 | This Regulation does not apply to AI systems where and in so far they are placed on the market, put into service, or used with or without modification exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities.
@ref Art 2(3) second subparagraph (src:44)
-- "where and in so far": a system with a mixed purpose is outside the exclusion for the part that serves another purpose; answer yes only where all of it is military, defence or national security.
@export Under Article 2(3), as an authorised representative, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system is placed on the market, put into service or used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system placed on the market, put into service or used, with or without modification, exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes? Answer no if it also serves any other purpose.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(3), as an authorised representative, does the Regulation apply to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` IS
    `Art 2(3) the Regulation applies to the AI system used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes` `the date asked` `the AI system is placed on the market, put into service or used exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes`


§ `Article 2(12): AI systems released under free and open-source licences`
-- Only if the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence.

-- src:56 | 12. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems released under free and open-source licences, unless they are placed on the market or put into service as high-risk AI systems or as an AI system that falls under Article 5 or 50.
@ref Art 2(12) (src:56)
-- The system is "placed on the market or put into service as a high-risk AI system" when its route is Article 6(1) with Annex I or Article 6(2) with Annex III (the keel's seam S1: high-risk if and only if the route is not `Route neither`).
-- Whether the system falls under Article 5 or Article 50 is decided in other provisions of the Regulation; here it is a yes/no fact.
@export Under Article 2(12), as an authorised representative, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system released under a free and open-source licence?
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the AI system falls under Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system fall under Article 5 (prohibited AI practices)?
      `the AI system falls under Article 50` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system fall under Article 50 (transparency obligations for certain AI systems)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(12), as an authorised representative, does the Regulation apply to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` IS
    `Art 2(12) the Regulation applies to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` `the date asked` `the AI system is released under a free and open-source licence` (NOT (`the route by which the AI system is high-risk` EQUALS `Route neither`)) `the AI system falls under Article 5` `the AI system falls under Article 50`


§ `Article 2(13): limiting the requirements for Article 6(1) systems (inserted by the Omnibus)`
-- Only if the AI system is high-risk under Article 6(1) and Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I applies to it.
-- The paragraph is in the text as amended only: before 27 July 2026 every answer is "not covered".

-- src:58 | 13. For high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(1), the application of specific requirements or obligations laid down in Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25 may be limited, where and to the extent that:
-- src:59 | (a) Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned; and
-- src:60 | (b) such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation.
-- src:61 | By 2 August 2027, the Commission shall adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to supplement this Regulation by specifying the high-risk AI systems concerned, the requirements or obligations that may be limited, the conditions under which such limitation applies, and the scope of the limitation.
@ref Art 2(13) (src:58-61)
-- A "may" gated by "where and to the extent that": when a condition fails the answer is JUST FALSE (fork F-2-13 of the keel; the other reading is NOTHING).
-- The Commission's delegated acts under the last sentence are the Commission's duty: no seat asks about it.
@export Under Article 2(13), as an authorised representative, may the application of the requirement or obligation I name be limited?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the number of the Article I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which Article of the Regulation do you ask about? Give its number, for example 9 for Article 9.
      `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any` IS A STRING @desc If the Article has a letter after its number, give it, for example a for Article 60a. Otherwise leave this empty.
      `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article` IS A NUMBER @desc Which paragraph of that Article do you ask about? Give its number, or 0 if you mean the whole Article.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations that provide an equivalent or higher level of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations that provide an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned?
      `such a limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would such a limitation leave the overall level of protection provided for by the Regulation unreduced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(13), as an authorised representative, may the application of the requirement or obligation I name be limited` IS
    `Art 2(13) the application of the requirement or obligation may be limited` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the requirement or obligation I ask about` `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations that provide an equivalent or higher level of protection` `such a limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`
    WHERE
        `the requirement or obligation I ask about` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
            number IS `the number of the Article I ask about`
            letter IS `the letter that follows the number of that Article, if any`
            paragraph IS `the number of the paragraph of that Article, or 0 for the whole Article`


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`
-- The role question of the seat: the other questions of this file assume the answer is yes.

-- src:70 | (5) ‘authorised representative’ means a natural or legal person located or established in the Union who has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model to, respectively, perform and carry out on its behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation;
@ref Art 3(5) (src:70)
-- The role question of this seat.
@export Under Article 3(5), as an authorised representative, does the definition of an authorised representative fit me?
GIVEN `my place of establishment or location` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you established or located in the Union, or in a third country?
      `I have received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model?
      `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the mandate to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by the Regulation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(5), as an authorised representative, does the definition of an authorised representative fit me` IS
    `Art 3(5) the party is an authorised representative` `my place of establishment or location` `I have received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation`

-- src:73 | (8) ‘operator’ means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor;
@ref Art 3(8) (src:73)
-- No fact is asked: the seat fixes the role passed to the keel (a person who holds another role asks that seat's question).
@export Under Article 3(8), as an authorised representative, am I an operator?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(8), as an authorised representative, am I an operator` IS
    `Art 3(8) the role is an operator` `Authorised representative`


§ `Article 111(1): components of large-scale IT systems listed in Annex X`
-- Only if the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system established by one of the twelve legal acts listed in Annex X, and was placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2027.
-- The text names no party that must bring the system into compliance: the keel reads it as the operator (fork F-111-1-party of the keel), so every operator seat asks it.

-- src:1620 | 1. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), AI systems which are components of the large-scale IT systems established by the legal acts listed in Annex X that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2027 shall be brought into compliance with this Regulation by 31 December 2030.
@ref Art 111(1) first subparagraph (src:1620)
-- Without prejudice to Article 5: this paragraph speaks of compliance with the Regulation as a whole.
@export Under Article 111(1), as an authorised representative, by what date must the AI system be brought into compliance with the Regulation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system a component of a large-scale IT system?
      `the act that establishes that large-scale IT system` IS A STRING @desc Which legal act established that large-scale IT system? Write it exactly as Annex X names it: Regulation (EU) 2018/1860, Regulation (EU) 2018/1861, Regulation (EU) 2018/1862, Regulation (EU) 2021/1133, Regulation (EU) 2021/1134, Regulation (EU) 2024/1358, Regulation (EU) 2017/2226, Regulation (EU) 2018/1240, Regulation (EU) 2018/1241, Regulation (EU) 2019/816, Regulation (EU) 2019/817 or Regulation (EU) 2019/818. If it is not a large-scale IT system, write none.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Article 111(1), as an authorised representative, by what date must the AI system be brought into compliance with the Regulation` IS
    `Art 111(1) the date by which the AI system must be brought into compliance` `the date asked` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` (`Annex X the large-scale IT system is established by a listed legal act` `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system` `the act that establishes that large-scale IT system`)

-- src:1620 | 1. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), AI systems which are components of the large-scale IT systems established by the legal acts listed in Annex X that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2027 shall be brought into compliance with this Regulation by 31 December 2030.
@ref Art 111(1) first subparagraph (src:1620)
-- The deadline is a computed WITHIN (31 December 2030 minus the day the Regulation enters into force), so the clock of a trace starts at 1 August 2024 (day 0).
-- A form shows an exported obligation as the placeholder "<obligation>"; the traces in the case file read the residual obligation.
@export Under Article 111(1), as an authorised representative, what must I do to bring the AI system into compliance on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system a component of a large-scale IT system?
      `the act that establishes that large-scale IT system` IS A STRING @desc Which legal act established that large-scale IT system? Write it exactly as Annex X names it: Regulation (EU) 2018/1860, Regulation (EU) 2018/1861, Regulation (EU) 2018/1862, Regulation (EU) 2021/1133, Regulation (EU) 2021/1134, Regulation (EU) 2024/1358, Regulation (EU) 2017/2226, Regulation (EU) 2018/1240, Regulation (EU) 2018/1241, Regulation (EU) 2019/816, Regulation (EU) 2019/817 or Regulation (EU) 2019/818. If it is not a large-scale IT system, write none.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 111 act`
DECIDE `Under Article 111(1), as an authorised representative, what must I do to bring the AI system into compliance on the date asked` IS
    `Art 111(1) the duty to bring the AI system into compliance` `the date asked` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` (`Annex X the large-scale IT system is established by a listed legal act` `the AI system is a component of a large-scale IT system` `the act that establishes that large-scale IT system`)


§ `Article 111(2), first sentence: is my high-risk AI system saved? (replaced by the Omnibus)`
-- Only if your AI system is high-risk and was placed on the market or put into service before the date from which Chapter III applies to it.
-- The question reads Chapter III Sections 1 to 3, the group whose date of application the sentence refers to; it is not asked about Article 5, which the sentence leaves untouched.

-- src:1623 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113, third paragraph, point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before the date of application of Chapter III referred to in Article 113, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159 | 2. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), this Regulation shall apply to operators of high-risk AI systems, other than the systems referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2026, only if, as from that date, those systems are subject to significant changes in their designs. In any case, the providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations of this Regulation by 2 August 2030.
@ref Art 111(2) first sentence (src:1623) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2159)
-- The keel offers the two texts of the saving as separate functions and no dispatcher (NEEDS-CORE.md): the question chooses between them with the keel's version function and does nothing else.
-- TRUE means the Regulation does not apply to the operator of this system under the "only if"; FALSE means the saving does not cover it (the keel's answer, passed through).
@export Under Article 111(2), as an authorised representative, is my high-risk AI system saved from the application of the Regulation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 111(2), as an authorised representative, is my high-risk AI system saved from the application of the Regulation` IS
    CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN `Art 111(2) as enacted the system is saved` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 111(2) as amended the system is saved` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`


§ `Article 111 and Article 113: does the group General apply on the date asked?`
-- The group General holds every provision that no point of Article 113 dates separately, among them Articles 111 to 113 themselves: it applies from 2 August 2026 (Art 113, second paragraph).
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1657 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2199 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
@ref Art 113 first and second paragraphs: the group General (Articles 111 to 113 and every provision no point of Article 113 dates) (src:1656-1657) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198-2199)
-- A legacy high-risk AI system saved by Article 111(2) is a separate question (Under Article 111(2), first sentence).
@export Under Article 111, as an authorised representative, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 111, as an authorised representative, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat rep from part P3 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P3-seat-rep: the questions of Articles 16 to 27 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744), asked as an authorised representative
-- A thin layer: every question calls one decision function of the layer-1 modules and restates no rule. The inputs that all questions of this part share carry the same name and the same description in every question.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not answer (the provision does not yet apply, the list is not closed, the provision limits itself, or the text points outside the sources).
-- The role questions and the applicability question come first; a caller that is not sure of the role asks the role question before the duty questions.

§ `Does the Regulation apply on the date asked`

@export Under Article 16, as an authorised representative, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 16, as an authorised representative, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` MEANS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Which party am I`

@export Under Article 16, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative within the meaning of Article 3(5)?
GIVEN `the party is located or established` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you located or established in the Union, or in a third country?
      `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model?
      `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the mandate to perform and carry out, on the provider's behalf, the obligations and procedures established by the Regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 16, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative within the meaning of Article 3(5)` MEANS
    JUST (`Art 3(5) the party is an authorised representative` `the party is located or established` `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation`)

§ `Article 22`

@export Under Article 22(3), as an authorised representative, do I perform the tasks specified in the mandate I received from the provider?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) and related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such a product.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1), does the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations that give an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation the question is about? Answer no if you do not know.
      `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the requirement or obligation the question is about leave the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation unreduced? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the authorised representative performs the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 22(3), as an authorised representative, do I perform the tasks specified in the mandate I received from the provider` MEANS
    `Art 22(3) the authorised representative performs the tasks specified in the mandate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` `the authorised representative performs the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the circumstances` MEANS `Section 3 circumstances` WITH
            `related to Section B products` IS `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Section A equivalent protection` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection`
            `no reduction of the overall level of protection` IS `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 22(3), as an authorised representative, have I provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) and related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such a product.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1), does the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations that give an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation the question is about? Answer no if you do not know.
      `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the requirement or obligation the question is about leave the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation unreduced? Answer no if you do not know.
      `a market surveillance authority has requested a copy of the mandate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a market surveillance authority has requested a copy of the mandate?
      `the authorised representative has provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities?
      `the copy is in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the copy is in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 22(3), as an authorised representative, have I provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request` MEANS
    `Art 22(3) the authorised representative has provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` `a market surveillance authority has requested a copy of the mandate` `the authorised representative has provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities` `the copy is in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the circumstances` MEANS `Section 3 circumstances` WITH
            `related to Section B products` IS `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Section A equivalent protection` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection`
            `no reduction of the overall level of protection` IS `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Article 22(3), as an authorised representative, does my mandate empower me to carry out the tasks listed in Article 22(3)(a) to (e) and to be addressed by the competent authorities?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) and related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such a product.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1), does the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations that give an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation the question is about? Answer no if you do not know.
      `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the requirement or obligation the question is about leave the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation unreduced? Answer no if you do not know.
      `verify the declaration of conformity, the technical documentation and the conformity assessment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your mandate empower you to verify the declaration of conformity, the technical documentation and the conformity assessment procedure?
      `keep at the disposal of the authorities for 10 years the provider's contact details, the declaration, the technical documentation and the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your mandate empower you to keep at the disposal of the authorities for 10 years the provider's contact details, the declaration, the technical documentation and the certificate?
      `provide a competent authority upon a reasoned request with all the information and documentation, including access to the logs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your mandate empower you to provide a competent authority upon a reasoned request with all the information and documentation, including access to the logs?
      `cooperate with competent authorities in any action in relation to the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your mandate empower you to cooperate with competent authorities in any action in relation to the high-risk AI system?
      `there are registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1) for the provider?
      `comply with the registration obligations or, if the provider registers, ensure the information is correct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your mandate empower you to comply with the registration obligations or, if the provider registers, ensure the information is correct?
      `be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities on all issues related to ensuring compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your mandate empower you to be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities on all issues related to ensuring compliance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 22(3), as an authorised representative, does my mandate empower me to carry out the tasks listed in Article 22(3)(a) to (e) and to be addressed by the competent authorities` MEANS
    `Art 22(3) the mandate empowers the authorised representative to carry out the tasks` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` `the mandate`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the circumstances` MEANS `Section 3 circumstances` WITH
            `related to Section B products` IS `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Section A equivalent protection` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection`
            `no reduction of the overall level of protection` IS `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`
        `the mandate` MEANS `Art 22(3) what the mandate empowers the authorised representative to do` OF `verify the declaration of conformity, the technical documentation and the conformity assessment procedure`, `keep at the disposal of the authorities for 10 years the provider's contact details, the declaration, the technical documentation and the certificate`, `provide a competent authority upon a reasoned request with all the information and documentation, including access to the logs`, `cooperate with competent authorities in any action in relation to the high-risk AI system`, `there are registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1)`, `comply with the registration obligations or, if the provider registers, ensure the information is correct`, `be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities on all issues related to ensuring compliance`

@export Under Article 22(4), as an authorised representative, have I terminated the mandate on considering that the provider is acting contrary to its obligations?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
