        `the circumstances` MEANS `Section 3 circumstances` WITH
            `related to Section B products` IS `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Section A equivalent protection` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection`
            `no reduction of the overall level of protection` IS `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat rep from part P4 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P4-seat-rep: the seat layer over the layer-1 modules of part P4 (Articles 28 to 39, Annex VII, Annex XIV of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: an authorised representative of a provider.
-- Each question below is one layer-1 function asked from this seat: it takes the facts this seat could state, as plain inputs (yes/no, a date, a number, or one of the keel's own choices),
-- each with an @desc, and calls the layer-1 function with them; nothing is restated here. A result of JUST TRUE is a yes, JUST FALSE is the text's no, and NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (including "this provision does not yet apply on the date asked, or does not apply to this AI system"): see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (P4)".
-- A question about the Articles of the group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` asks the date asked only (Annex XIV too); a question about Annex VII also asks the route, the placement date and the
-- change flag, because Article 111(2) can save a high-risk AI system placed on the market earlier and unchanged, and two more facts for Article 2(2): whether the products are covered by the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I,
-- and whether the requirements of the Regulation have been integrated in it. For a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with such products an Annex VII question answers JUST FALSE: Article 2(2) lets only Article 6(1),
-- Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 apply, so Article 43 and Annex VII do not (fork F-S14-reach).
-- Official powers and duties appear only as what they mean to this seat; there is never a seat for a notifying authority or the Commission.

§ `The role`

-- The facts that make this person an authorised representative, asked once; the other questions do not re-ask them. The keel's own definition does the work.
@export Under Annex VII point 3.1, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative within the meaning of Article 3(5)?
GIVEN `the party is located or established` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you located or established in the Union, or in a third country?
      `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model?
      `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the mandate to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Annex VII point 3.1, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative within the meaning of Article 3(5)` IS
    JUST (`Art 3(5) the party is an authorised representative` `the party is located or established` `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation`)

§ `Applicability: Annex VII`

@export Under Annex VII point 1, as an authorised representative, does the group General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Annex VII point 1, as an authorised representative, does the group General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Annex VII the group of Article 43 applies to the AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Annex VII point 3: the quality management system`

-- Annex VII point 3.1(a): the layer-1 function `Annex VII point 3.1(a) the application includes the name and address of the provider and of the authorised representative`
@export Under Annex VII point 3.1(a), as an authorised representative, does the application I lodged include the name and address of the provider and my own?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
