-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat rep from part P7 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P7-seat-rep: THE SEAT LAYER for an authorised representative of a provider, over the layer-1 modules of Articles 57 to 71 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: the authorised representative. In this part the text addresses it in two places: the provider's testing in real world conditions requires the provider to be established in the Union
-- or to have appointed a legal representative established in the Union (Article 60(4)(d), read as the authorised representative of Article 3(5): fork F-60-4-d); and the EU database data of
-- Sections A and B of Annex VIII are entered by the provider "or, where applicable, by the authorised representative" (Article 71(2)). Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, one of the keel's own choices, each with an @desc. The date asked comes first. `General` applies from 2 August 2026.
-- Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

§ `Under Article 57: the group General and the role`

-- The applicability question for the provision group `General` that Article 57 opens in this part's range: it asks only the date, and passes the core's constants for the route, the placement date and the change.
@export Under Article 57, as an authorised representative, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as an authorised representative, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- The role question. Article 3(5) defines the authorised representative: whoever is located or established in the Union and has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by the Regulation. The other questions of this seat assume you hold this role.
@export Under Article 57, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative?
GIVEN `the party is located or established` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you located or established in the Union, or in a third country?
      `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model?
      `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the mandate to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by the Regulation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative` IS
    `Art 3(5) the party is an authorised representative` `the party is located or established` `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation`


§ `Under Article 60: the provider's testing in real world conditions`

-- Article 60(4)(d). The text says "legal representative"; it is read as the authorised representative (fork F-60-4-d).
@export Under Article 60, as an authorised representative, is the condition of Article 60(4)(d) met, because the provider is established in the Union or has appointed a legal representative established in the Union, such as me?
GIVEN `the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provider or prospective provider that conducts the testing established in the Union?
      `the provider or prospective provider has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the provider or prospective provider appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union (for example you)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as an authorised representative, is the condition of Article 60(4)(d) met, because the provider is established in the Union or has appointed a legal representative established in the Union, such as me` IS
    `Art 60(4)(d) the provider is established in the Union or has appointed a legal representative established in the Union` `the provider or prospective provider conducting the testing is established in the Union` `the provider or prospective provider has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union`


§ `Under Article 71: the EU database`

-- Article 71(2): by the provider or, where applicable, by the authorised representative.
@export Under Article 71, as an authorised representative, have the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII been entered into the EU database, by the provider or, where applicable, by me as the authorised representative?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the provider enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the provider enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database? Answer yes or no.
      `the authorised representative enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the authorised representative enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 71, as an authorised representative, have the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII been entered into the EU database, by the provider or, where applicable, by me as the authorised representative` IS
    `Art 71(2) the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII have been entered into the EU database` `the date asked` `the provider enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database` `the authorised representative enters the data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII into the EU database`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat rep from part P8 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P8 seat layer: an authorised representative of a provider: what the AI Office and the market surveillance authorities may do to an operator, and what an operator must do under Articles 74 to 79.
-- SEAT: an authorised representative
--
-- Nothing here is new law: each question calls the layer-1 function of Articles 72 to 79 (P8-art72 to P8-art79) that answers it, and the keel
-- (aia-definitions, aia-timeline, aia-core) for the role facts and the dates. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, a number or
-- one of the keel's own choices, each with an @desc worded for the person asking. A question answers JUST value, or NOTHING where the text does
-- not decide it (the Regulation does not apply yet on the date asked, or the text is silent); a JUST FALSE is a "no" the text itself gives.
-- Questions are grouped by Article in the order of the text; the role question and the applicability questions come first.


§ `The role the person asking holds`

-- The role, worked out by the keel's definition; the other questions of this seat assume it.
@export Under Article 74, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative within the meaning of Article 3(5)?
GIVEN `the party is located or established` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you established or located in the Union, or in a third country?
      `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model?
      `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the mandate to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by the Regulation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 74, as an authorised representative, am I an authorised representative within the meaning of Article 3(5)` IS
    `Art 3(5) the party is an authorised representative` `the party is located or established` `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation`

§ `Which provisions apply on the date asked`

-- Calls the gate helper of P8-gate, which passes the group to the keel's `Art 113 the provision group applies`.
@export Under Article 72, as an authorised representative, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 72, as an authorised representative, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Article 74: Market surveillance and control of AI systems in the Union market`
-- Arises only when a market surveillance authority acts on the AI system; the access questions arise only after its request.

-- Calls `Art 74(1)(a) the party is understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020`.
@export Under Article 74(1), as an authorised representative, am I understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 74(1), as an authorised representative, am I understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` IS
    `Art 74(1)(a) the party is understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` `the date asked` `Authorised representative`

§ `Article 75a: Supervisory and enforcement powers of the AI Office`
-- Arises only if the AI Office is supervising or enforcing against the operator.

-- Calls `Art 75a(1) second sentence the AI Office is authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities`.
@export Under Article 75a(1), as an authorised representative, is the AI Office authorised to fully reclaim from me the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance?
      `the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75a(1), as an authorised representative, is the AI Office authorised to fully reclaim from me the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities` IS
    `Art 75a(1) second sentence the AI Office is authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities` `the date asked` `the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance` `the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator`

-- Calls `Art 75a(2) second sentence the AI Office must notify the operator of the AI system concerned`.
@export Under Article 75a(2), as an authorised representative, must the AI Office notify me as the operator of the AI system concerned?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI Office has started an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the AI Office has started an investigation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75a(2), as an authorised representative, must the AI Office notify me as the operator of the AI system concerned` IS
    `Art 75a(2) second sentence the AI Office must notify the operator of the AI system concerned` `the date asked` `the AI Office has started an investigation`

-- Calls `Art 75a(3) first subparagraph the AI Office may exercise the powers listed in Article 14(4), points (a), (b) and (c) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(12) and (13) by simple request or by decision`.
