    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

§ `Under Article 99(4)(b)`

@ref Art 99(4)(b)
@export Under Article 99(4)(b), as an authorised representative, is my non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22 subject to administrative fines?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I to the Regulation? Answer no if you do not know. This matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Answer no if you do not know. It decides nothing about the Articles asked here (it matters only to Articles 57, 58 and 59), but the same question is asked of every provision that Article 2(2) can cut off.
      `the non-compliance or the supply is established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the non-compliance (or the supply of the information) been established?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 99(4)(b), as an authorised representative, is my non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22 subject to administrative fines` IS
    `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 99(4)(b) non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22` `the non-compliance or the supply is established`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

@ref Art 99(4)(b)
@export Under Article 99(4)(b), as an authorised representative, what is the ceiling of the administrative fine for my non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the offender is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offender an undertaking?
      `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year, in euros?
      `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offender a small or medium-sized enterprise, including a start-up?
      `the offender is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offender a small mid-cap enterprise (SMC)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 99(4)(b), as an authorised representative, what is the ceiling of the administrative fine for my non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22` IS
    `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` `the date asked` `Art 99(4)(b) non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22` `the offender is an undertaking` `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` `the offender is an SMC`
